---
title: Sri Lankan Dhal Curry
servings: 4
---

Wash @split red lentils{360%g} until water is clear.

Add @roasted Sri Lankan curry powder{1%tsp}, @unroasted Sri Lankan curry powder{2%tsp}, @turmeric{2%tsp}, @curry leaves{handful}, @garlic{1%clove}(crushed) and @chilli powder{1%tsp} to the washed red lentils.

Add @water{} to cover the red lentils and about half an inch more, then bring to a boil.

Once lentils are half boiled, add @coconut milk{1%can} and keep stirring. Add @salt{} to taste.

Cook until lentils are soft (but not too soft) on medium heat.
